Description: Bande desktop environment
 The Bande desktop: a pure Wayland desktop with its own compositor, shell,
 session services and applications. Installing this package adds "Bande"
 to the sessions a display manager such as GDM, SDDM or greetd offers.
 .
 It recommends a browser, text editor, image viewer, PDF viewer, calculator
 and video player, and opens files in them by default, an unlocked keyring
 for the passwords browsers and editors keep, fallback fonts for every
 script and the print service.
 .
 So that running out of memory never freezes the computer, it recommends
 compressed swap in memory (zram, sized like Fedora's and compressed with
 zstd) and systemd-oomd, and makes the apps' slice the place where
 systemd-oomd closes an app when memory stays under pressure, so the
 compositor and the session services keep running.
